<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Web Development Standards Implementation</title>

<style>
*{
    margin:0;
    padding:0;
    box-sizing:border-box;
    font-family:'Segoe UI',sans-serif;
}

body{
    background:#f5f7fb;
    color:#333;
    line-height:1.6;
}

/* Header */
header{
    background:linear-gradient(135deg,#0077ff,#00c6ff);
    color:white;
    text-align:center;
    padding:60px 20px;
}

header h1{
    font-size:42px;
}

header p{
    margin-top:15px;
    font-size:18px;
}

/* Navigation */

nav{
    background:#0a2342;
    position:sticky;
    top:0;
    z-index:1000;
}

nav ul{
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    list-style:none;
}

nav li{
    margin:15px;
}

nav a{
    color:white;
    text-decoration:none;
    font-weight:bold;
}

nav a:hover{
    color:#00c6ff;
}

/* Sections */

.container{
    width:90%;
    max-width:1200px;
    margin:auto;
}

section{
    background:white;
    margin:35px 0;
    padding:30px;
    border-radius:12px;
    box-shadow:0px 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,.1);
}

h2{
    color:#0077ff;
    margin-bottom:20px;
}

/* Cards */

.grid{
    display:grid;
    grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(250px,1fr));
    gap:20px;
}

.card{
    background:#eef6ff;
    padding:20px;
    border-radius:10px;
    border-left:6px solid #0077ff;
    transition:.3s;
}

.card:hover{
    transform:translateY(-5px);
}

/* Table */

table{
    width:100%;
    border-collapse:collapse;
}

table th{
    background:#0077ff;
    color:white;
}

table th,
table td{
    padding:12px;
    border:1px solid #ddd;
}

/* Video */

.video{
    text-align:center;
}

video{
    width:90%;
    max-width:700px;
    border-radius:10px;
}

/* Answers */

.answer{
    background:#e9fff0;
    padding:18px;
    border-left:6px solid green;
    margin:15px 0;
}

/* Footer */

footer{
    background:#0a2342;
    color:white;
    text-align:center;
    padding:20px;
    margin-top:30px;
}
</style>

</head>
<body>

<header>

<h1>🌐 Web Development Standards Implementation</h1>

<p>Scenario Based Learning using HTML5, HTTP, XML and Web Communication Protocols</p>

</header>

<nav>

<ul>

<li><a href="#scenario">Scenario</a></li>

<li><a href="#video">Video</a></li>

<li><a href="#snippets">Data</a></li>

<li><a href="#questions">Questions</a></li>

<li><a href="#answers">Answers</a></li>

</ul>

</nav>

<div class="container">

<section id="scenario">

<h2>📖 Scenario</h2>

<p>
A startup company is developing a modern web application.
During development, the developers encounter problems related to
HTML elements, HTTP methods, XML syntax, and web communication protocols.
They must select the correct web standards to build a secure,
responsive, and standards-compliant website.
</p>

<br>

<div class="grid">

<div class="card">
<h3>🎥 Homepage</h3>
Embed a promotional video.
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>📝 Registration</h3>
Securely send user data to the server.
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>🧭 Navigation</h3>
Use semantic HTML elements.
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>📄 XML</h3>
Fix configuration syntax errors.
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>🌐 Protocol</h3>
Use the correct communication protocol.
</div>

</div>

</section>

<section id="video">

<h2>🎥 Promotional Video</h2>

<div class="video">

<video controls>
<source src="video.mp4" type="video/mp4">
Your browser does not support HTML5 Video.
</video>

<p><br>This demonstrates the correct HTML5
<strong>&lt;video&gt;</strong> element.</p>

</div>

</section>

<section id="snippets">

<h2>📋 Data Snippets</h2>

<table>

<tr>

<th>Category</th>

<th>Options</th>

</tr>

<tr>

<td>Video Tag</td>

<td>

A. &lt;media&gt;<br>

<b>B. &lt;video src="video.mp4" controls&gt;&lt;/video&gt;</b><br>

C. &lt;movie&gt;<br>

D. &lt;vid&gt;

</td>

</tr>

<tr>

<td>HTTP Method</td>

<td>

GET | <b>POST</b> | PUT | DELETE

</td>

</tr>

<tr>

<td>Navigation</td>

<td>

&lt;div&gt; |
<b>&lt;nav&gt;</b> |
&lt;section&gt; |
&lt;header&gt;

</td>

</tr>

<tr>

<td>XML</td>

<td>

<b>&lt;note&gt;&lt;to&gt;User&lt;/to&gt;&lt;from&gt;Admin&lt;/from&gt;&lt;/note&gt;</b>

</td>

</tr>

<tr>

<td>Protocol</td>

<td>

FTP |
<b>HTTP</b> |
SMTP |
SNMP

</td>

</tr>

</table>

</section>

<section id="questions">

<h2>❓ Questions</h2>

<ol>

<li>Select the correct HTML tag for video embedding and justify your answer.</li>

<li>Identify the appropriate HTTP method for form submission and explain why.</li>

<li>Choose the proper semantic HTML element for navigation.</li>

<li>Identify the correct XML syntax and explain errors in the remaining options.</li>

<li>Select the correct web communication protocol and justify your answer.</li>

</ol>

</section>

<section id="answers">

<h2>✅ Solutions</h2>

<div class="answer">

<h3>1. Video Embedding</h3>

<p><b>Answer:</b> &lt;video&gt;</p>

<p>The HTML5 <b>&lt;video&gt;</b> tag is specifically designed for embedding videos. The controls attribute provides Play, Pause, Volume, and Fullscreen buttons.</p>

</div>

<div class="answer">

<h3>2. HTTP Method</h3>

<p><b>Answer:</b> POST</p>

<p>POST sends user information inside the request body, making it more secure than GET for registration forms.</p>

</div>

<div class="answer">

<h3>3. Semantic Navigation</h3>

<p><b>Answer:</b> &lt;nav&gt;</p>

<p>The navigation element clearly defines menus and improves accessibility and SEO.</p>

</div>

<div class="answer">

<h3>4. XML Syntax</h3>

<p><b>Answer:</b></p>

<code>
&lt;note&gt;
&lt;to&gt;User&lt;/to&gt;
&lt;from&gt;Admin&lt;/from&gt;
&lt;/note&gt;
</code>

<p><br>Other options contain missing closing tags, mismatched tags, or incomplete syntax.</p>

</div>

<div class="answer">

<h3>5. Communication Protocol</h3>

<p><b>Answer:</b> HTTP</p>

<p>HTTP (HyperText Transfer Protocol) is the standard protocol used by browsers and web servers to exchange web pages and application data.</p>

</div>

</section>

</div>

<footer>

<h3>Internet Programming Project</h3>

<p>Designed using HTML5 & CSS3 | Web Development Standards Implementation</p>

</footer>

</body>
</html>